<figure class="cache-figure" data-local-cache-reuse>
 <p class="figure-title">Reuse pays for the copies and their invalidations</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Application processes <input data-processes type="range" min="1" max="12" value="4" /><output data-processes-label>4</output></label><label>Reads per process between updates <input data-reads type="range" min="1" max="20" value="10" /><output data-reads-label>10</output></label></div>
 <div class="local-processes" data-process-copies></div>
 <div class="cache-stat-row local-reuse-stats"><div><strong data-baseline>40</strong><span>Redis reads without L1</span></div><div><strong data-redis>4</strong><span>Redis reads with L1</span></div><div><strong data-invalidations>4</strong><span>invalidation deliveries</span></div><div><strong data-memory>8 KiB</strong><span>duplicated local allocation</span></div></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>One repeating cycle: update the shared key, deliver its invalidation to every process, then each process reads it sequentially. The first read repopulates and re-registers the copy; later reads hit L1. Each local copy is assumed to allocate 2 KiB including overhead. Counts are per cycle, not a throughput benchmark; a read command and an invalidation do not necessarily have equal byte or CPU cost.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{reuseCycle}from'../../lib/caching/tracking.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-local-cache-reuse]').forEach(root=>{const processes=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-processes]')!,reads=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-reads]')!;const render=()=>{const s=reuseCycle(Number(processes.value),Number(reads.value));root.querySelector('[data-processes-label]')!.textContent=String(s.processes);root.querySelector('[data-reads-label]')!.textContent=String(s.reads);root.querySelector('[data-process-copies]')!.replaceChildren(...Array.from({length:s.processes},(_,i)=>{const tile=document.createElement('div');const name=document.createElement('b');name.textContent=`Process ${i+1}`;const copy=document.createElement('span');copy.textContent='Local copy · 2 KiB';const hits=document.createElement('small');hits.textContent=`1 Redis read · ${s.reads-1} local hits`;tile.append(name,copy,hits);return tile;}));for(const[key,value]of[['baseline',s.requests],['redis',s.redisReads],['invalidations',s.invalidations],['memory',`${s.localKiB} KiB`]]as const)root.querySelector(`[data-${key}]`)!.textContent=String(value);root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.hits===0?'Every read follows an update, so L1 saves no Redis reads. It still retains copies and processes invalidations.':`${s.hits} of ${s.requests} reads stay local (${Math.round(s.hitRate*100)}%). Each process still needs one Redis read and one invalidation per cycle. More processes multiply both the copies and this baseline work.`;};processes.oninput=render;reads.oninput=render;render();});
</script>
